// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//
// Phase C2 operator gate: qkv_proj.
//
// One GEMM over the full 3*emb_dim fused weight, with C split three ways by
// three cast launches so Q, K and V land in separate DDR buffers without a
// host-side slice. Tiles and method come from kernel_registry, which raises
// rather than guessing on an unmeasured shape -- so a shape that is not in the
// registry fails here loudly instead of running with a hand-copied tiling.
//
// Runs opcheck.py on real NPU2 against an FP32 reference: np.isclose over the
// full output at rtol=1.6e-2, zero permitted mismatches, across all three
// outputs. Not cosine similarity -- kernel_registry/README.md is explicit that
// a correlation gate is blind to a systematic per-element scale error.
//
// All three registered shapes run, and all three are checked. The three
// precision lines per shape are checked individually and in order: a build that
// wired all three split-cast launches at the same column offset would still emit
// three outputs and still pass a check that only looked at the verdict, so
// requiring three distinct precision reports and then the named operator and
// shape makes the shape of the evidence part of the gate.
//
// The third shape is the study's 64x768x2304, and it is here because a registry
// resolution check cannot show that a row computes the right thing. That shape
// was registered with `drain` and `direct` only while this builder pins
// fused-cast, so the operator raised on it; the fused-cast configuration the
// sweep later found for it replaced one that returned zeros for two of the nine
// sub-tiles of each cast worker. It is also the only point here whose herd is
// not the file-level 8x4, M = 64 being too short to hold 8 rows of fused-cast's
// forced tile_m -- so it is the one shape that fails if the per-row herd stops
// being wired through the lookup.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipe below. Device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock, which XRTRunner.run_test holds across
// binary load and dispatch (python/air/backend/xrt_runner.py:292) -- the same
// inode lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution and KernelCache take, so this interlocks
// with every other NPU job in the repository while the peano compiles still
// overlap. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here instead would DEADLOCK:
// the gate command that invokes this suite already holds that inode, and BSD
// flock(2) treats a second open() of the same file as a foreign lock, so the
// nested acquire would block against its own parent until the timeout expires.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_qkv_proj_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_qkv_proj_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-qkv-proj PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: [precision] Output 0
// CHECK: [precision] Output 1
// CHECK: [precision] Output 2
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] qkv_proj [2048x1024]: PASS
// CHECK: [precision] Output 0
// CHECK: [precision] Output 1
// CHECK: [precision] Output 2
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] qkv_proj [2048x2048]: PASS
// CHECK: QKV GEMM 64x768x2304 (fused-cast, registry{{.*}}herd=1x4)
// CHECK: [precision] Output 0
// CHECK: [precision] Output 1
// CHECK: [precision] Output 2
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] qkv_proj [64x768]: PASS
// The fourth is Phase D1's: the same 768 width at the sequence length the block
// runs, 4096. The herd is back to the file-level 8x4 here -- M = 4096 holds 8
// rows of fused-cast's tile_m -- so this shape and the 64-row one above are the
// two ends of the per-row herd wiring and both are checked.
// CHECK: QKV GEMM 4096x768x2304 (fused-cast, registry{{.*}}herd=8x4)
// CHECK: [precision] Output 0
// CHECK: [precision] Output 1
// CHECK: [precision] Output 2
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] qkv_proj [4096x768]: PASS
